---
// src/pages/bucknell/index.astro  →  arizvi.com/bucknell
// For the Bucknell business analytics search (Analytics & Operations Management, Freeman College of Management).
// The page is Meowdle, the mock Moodle, and nothing else (Ali, 19 Nov 2026: "i think we should remove all the
// commentary and just leave Meow-Dle", then, after the cold reads that night, "Meowdle" and "Remove them all" for the
// lines inside it that spoke to the committee). No title, lede or section heading above it, and nothing in it about
// the visit. Meowdle's name, across the top of the shell, is the page's h1, and the tab reads as Moodle's would
// ("Course: ANOP 102 | Meowdle").
// Meowdle opens on the class Ali teaches on his campus visit (Ali, 17 Nov 2026: "For Bucknell, focus on building out a
// mock LMS around the one lesson that I am teaching"): ANOP 102, week 11, class 2, "Playlists or radio?"
// (MoodleShell.astro, content in src/data/bucknell102.ts, the regression in SongsDemo.astro). Bucknell set the topic:
// multiple linear regression, at the level of ANOP 102. Since 19 Nov the class's plan follows the deck he teaches from
// for minutes 5 to 35 ("Follow the deck in the plan only").
// The lesson is his of 17 Nov 2026 (the same class runs at Tulane): the 150 top-ranked songs released from January
// 2023 to early June 2024 in the Kaggle dataset, gaps in the data left out, radio against playlists.
// Bucknell's orange (the section colour) marks where you are in Meowdle, what the student has done, and a rubric's
// best level.
// The course pages (/bucknell/anop-102/ and its pack, ANOP 302, 330 and 400) go with this page; ANOP 102's is linked
// from the shell's syllabus. Not linked from the nav; sends noindex.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import MoodleShell from '../../components/MoodleShell.astro';
import { bucknellColours } from '../../data/bucknell';
---
<Base title="Course: ANOP 102 | Meowdle" description="Playlists or radio? The multiple regression class Ali Rizvi teaches on his Bucknell campus visit, for ANOP 102, laid out in Meowdle, a mock Moodle." noindex accent={bucknellColours}>
  <MoodleShell start="mdl-class2" />
</Base>
